WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.581
Ally fidgeted nervously as she waited for Lainie's assistant to answer the phone.

2
00:00:05.582 --> 00:00:08.110
"Lainie Polk's office, may I help you?"

3
00:00:08.111 --> 00:00:11.862
"Hello, this is Ally." Ally paused.

4
00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:14.693
She really didn't want to be making this call.

5
00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:18.913
"I'm calling because . . . because I can't go to—"

6
00:00:18.914 --> 00:00:22.380
Bong! It was the sound of Alpha booting up.

7
00:00:22.381 --> 00:00:26.572
"Alpha reporting for duty!" she announced loudly.

8
00:00:26.573 --> 00:00:30.813
"Shh, Alpha, I'm on the phone," Ally whispered.

9
00:00:30.814 --> 00:00:33.447
"Anyway, I'm calling because I—"

10
00:00:33.448 --> 00:00:37.782
"I have retrieved an answer to your problem, Allyzooba!" Alpha boomed.

11
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:40.342
"You have?" Ally said.

12
00:00:40.343 --> 00:00:42.849
"What's that?" Lainie's assistant said.

13
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.006
"What were you saying, Ally?"

14
00:00:45.007 --> 00:00:50.625
"Uh, nothing. I'll, um, call you back later. Thanks!"

15
00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:56.033
Ally raced over to Alpha. "So, what's the answer?"

16
00:00:56.034 --> 00:01:01.773
"It is possible to travel Earth without a passport under certain conditions," Alpha said.

17
00:01:01.774 --> 00:01:05.131
"What conditions are those?" Ally asked.

18
00:01:05.132 --> 00:01:09.671
"Humans must have a passport to cross the border into another country."

19
00:01:09.672 --> 00:01:13.934
"I know that!" Ally was getting impatient.

20
00:01:13.935 --> 00:01:23.933
"I believe, as long as you do not leave the tarmac and go through customs, no one will check your ID or ask to see your passport," Alpha said. "It

21
00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:28.490
should be safe if you stay near the plane and don’t enter the airport." "Alpha!

22
00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:35.522
You're a genius!" Ally went to hug Alpha, but Alpha blared a warning sound. "Halt,

23
00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:47.475
Allyzooba! You have been warned before. Hugs are for Earthlings!" ***

24
00:01:47.476 --> 00:01:54.030
Ally watched out the window as Lainie's private jet touched down on the runway in Patagonia.

25
00:01:54.031 --> 00:01:59.395
"I can't believe I'm here!" she thought. "I made it!"

26
00:01:59.396 --> 00:02:04.126
As soon as the plane stopped, she raced down the stairs and onto the tarmac.

27
00:02:04.127 --> 00:02:07.583
Lainie was standing next to a Jeep.

28
00:02:07.584 --> 00:02:12.164
"Welcome to Patagonia, Ally!" Lainie said.

29
00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:17.848
"You've got great timing. There's an eclipse today, and it's about to start.

30
00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:20.657
Here, put on some goggles."

31
00:02:20.658 --> 00:02:24.478
"I don't think I need those," Ally said.

32
00:02:24.479 --> 00:02:27.574
"Of course, you do," Lainie insisted.

33
00:02:27.575 --> 00:02:32.268
"It's not safe to look at an eclipse with the bare human eye."

34
00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:35.430
"Right! Thanks, Lainie."

35
00:02:35.431 --> 00:02:41.916
As Ally and Lainie gazed up at the sky through the goggles, the sun began to disappear behind the moon.

36
00:02:41.917 --> 00:02:46.648
"I hope this works," Ally thought, taking a deep breath.

37
00:02:46.649 --> 00:02:50.938
As the eclipse continued, a strange sensation washed over her.

38
00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:54.671
It felt like being tickled, followed by chills.

39
00:02:54.672 --> 00:02:58.335
"Is it happening?" Ally thought. She couldn't tell.

40
00:02:58.336 --> 00:03:03.510
"I know! I'll test my powers by trying to read Lainie's thoughts."

41
00:03:03.511 --> 00:03:07.251
Ally concentrated as hard as she could.

42
00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:12.519
She was ready to be disappointed when suddenly she saw Lainie thinking about the eclipse.

43
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:20.409
Lainie was wondering if she could use some of her billions to create a machine that would create eclipses on demand.

44
00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.846
"My powers are back!" Ally thought.

45
00:03:23.847 --> 00:03:35.574
Then she laughed to herself. "That's such a Lainie thing to think!"

46
00:03:35.575 --> 00:03:38.428
A moment later Lainie turned to her.

47
00:03:38.429 --> 00:03:43.804
"We'd better get going. It's a long drive to my research camp."

48
00:03:43.805 --> 00:03:46.088
"Um . . ." Ally froze.

49
00:03:46.089 --> 00:03:51.595
"Actually, I . . . I can't go with you. I forgot my passport."

50
00:03:51.596 --> 00:03:57.106
"What?" Lainie stared at Ally as if she had two heads.

51
00:03:57.107 --> 00:04:00.745
"You forgot your passport?"

52
00:04:00.746 --> 00:04:04.744
Ally nodded, afraid to hear what Lainie would say next.

53
00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:11.114
But to her surprise, Lainie burst out laughing.

54
00:04:11.115 --> 00:04:15.949
"Oh wow, Ally! You're as forgetful as I am!

55
00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:21.356
My pilot will take you back home, and you can see the penguins another time.

56
00:04:21.357 --> 00:04:24.863
At least you got to see the eclipse!" "Thank

57
00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:31.253
you," Ally said. "I really appreciate everything." She

58
00:04:31.254 --> 00:04:36.770
hugged Lainie, and then raced up the steps and back onto the jet. She'd

59
00:04:36.771 --> 00:04:40.573
just put on her seat belt when she got a text. Julius:

60
00:04:40.574 --> 00:04:43.387
Hey, what are you up to today? Ally:

61
00:04:43.388 --> 00:04:48.887
Oh, nothing much. What about you? A

62
00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:58.408
minute later the plane took off, and she was on her way back to Sandville. ***

63
00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:03.376
Alpha blinked awake. "Alert! Alert!"

64
00:05:03.377 --> 00:05:06.336
Mateo raced into Ally's room.

65
00:05:06.337 --> 00:05:11.088
"Shh, Alpha, you'll wake Papi!

66
00:05:11.089 --> 00:05:13.674
Ally will be back soon from Patagonia.

67
00:05:13.675 --> 00:05:15.639
What are you upset about?"

68
00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:18.403
Alpha's eyes looked wide and startled.

69
00:05:18.404 --> 00:05:21.987
"My sensors have detected an anomaly in Sandville!"

70
00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:28.323
Mateo frowned. "What are you talking about? What's an anomaly?"

71
00:05:28.324 --> 00:05:30.845
"An anomaly is something unusual.

72
00:05:30.846 --> 00:05:33.316
And this is very unusual.

73
00:05:33.317 --> 00:05:37.799
An alien life-form from the Jorganda Region in the vicinity."

74
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.953
"Wait, Alpha. Is that good news?" Mateo asked.

75
00:05:41.954 --> 00:05:45.634
"Do they have a ship? Can they take Ally home?"

76
00:05:45.635 --> 00:05:48.221
"They could do that," Alpha said.

77
00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:51.061
"But it is highly unlikely they would.

78
00:05:51.062 --> 00:06:00.945
In galactic year 874303, Jorganda made a vow—to destroy Astralia!"

